      },
      "question": {
        ":question/problem": "Given that $a=\u27e84,2,-4\u27e9,$ $b=\u27e8-3,-1,-4\u27e9,$ and $c=\u27e83,5,-4\u27e9,$ find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ using the definition of the scalar triple product.\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "First, we find the cross product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b\\times c & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 5 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -4 \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-3 & -4 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-1)\\cdot (-4)-(-4)\\cdot 5)i-((-3)\\cdot (-4)-3\\cdot (-4))j+((-3)\\cdot 5-(-1)\\cdot 3)k \\\\  & =24i-24j-12k \\\\  & =\u27e824,-24,-12\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the scalar triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =\u27e84,2,-4\u27e9\\cdot \u27e824,-24,-12\u27e9 \\\\  & =4\\cdot 24+2\\cdot (-24)+(-4)\\cdot (-12) \\\\  & =96-48+48 \\\\  & =96\\end{aligned}\n$$",
